  "question": {
    "text": "<p>As shown in the figure, a particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is placed at a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>.</mo></math> When the particle is slightly displaced to its right, it starts moving and reaches the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The speed of the particle at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. (Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> to the nearest integer is</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0100_83066cd91fd2.png\" style=\"width: 280px; height: 149px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "10",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Using work-energy theorem, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>.</mo></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>)</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>."
  }
